# PMT quantum efficiency table for sim_lighttrap (geometry.pmtQEFile / /detector/pmtQEFile / pmt_qe=)
#
# Format: two columns "<wavelength_nm> <QE>", QE as a fraction (0..1) or in percent
# (if any value is > 1 the whole table is read as %). Lines starting with '#' and
# blank lines are ignored; rows may be in any order; QE = 0 outside the tabulated range.
#
# ILLUSTRATIVE curve for a Hamamatsu R6836 (Cs-Te, MgF2 window, "200M" response,
# 115-320 nm). The only datasheet number is the typical cathode radiant sensitivity
# 28 mA/W at 254 nm -> QE = S * 1239.84 / lambda = 13.7 %. The rest of the shape is a
# generic Cs-Te solar-blind curve scaled to that point. REPLACE with the measured /
# vendor QE curve of your tube before using the results quantitatively.
#
# wl_nm   QE
 110     0.000
 115     0.040
 120     0.065
 130     0.090
 140     0.105
 160     0.120
 180     0.130
 200     0.135
 220     0.138
 240     0.138
 254     0.137
 270     0.125
 290     0.085
 300     0.055
 310     0.025
 320     0.008
 330     0.002
 340     0.000
